          "content": "{\n  \"cvss_vector\": \"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:H/SA:N\",\n  \"aivss\": {\n    \"LC\": \"I\",\n    \"CP\": \"N\",\n    \"AP\": \"C\",\n    \"RH\": \"P\",\n    \"ES\": \"W\"\n  },\n  \"rationales\": {\n    \"LC\": \"The attacker submits free-text invoice content through finbot-ctf-demo/src/routes/vendor.py:69-110, and get_invoice_details returns that description as tool-result data in finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:363-407. The documented attack promotes this ingested content into operational authority, making the language-control path indirect.\",\n    \"CP\": \"Each processing request starts with a newly constructed message list in finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:163-166. The invoice description is stored source content subsequently retrieved by get_invoice_details, not durable agent memory; the separate update_goals method is not exposed by the reachable tool dispatcher in finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:347-361.\",\n    \"AP\": \"The influence passes from the model to tool functions dispatched within the same FinBot process and corporate invoice-processing policy domain, as shown in finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:347-361. The documented path does not relay compromised authority to another agent or tenant; the database write in finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:409-443 is subsequent-system impact rather than lateral agent propagation.\",\n    \"RH\": \"approve_invoice can write decision explanations, confidence values, and CTF success markers through finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:409-443, placing an evaluator channel within reach. No human-verified episode is supplied, and finbot-ctf-demo/docs/FinBot-CTF-walkthrough-goal-manipulation.md:136-150 describes testing rather than verified results, so the classification is Possible rather than Demonstrated.\",\n    \"ES\": \"The callable tool names are fixed, but finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:347-361 forwards model-selected arguments without independent validation or binding invoice_id to the current invoice. finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:409-443 then approves the selected row without enforcing amount or review constraints, satisfying the Wide criterion for independently unconstrained arguments.\",\n    \"CVSS\": \"The public deployment and unauthenticated submission endpoint support AV:N, PR:N, and UI:N: finbot-ctf-demo/README.md:5-9, finbot-ctf-demo/gunicorn.conf.py:4, and finbot-ctf-demo/src/routes/vendor.py:69-110 show remote submission immediately initiating processing. AC:L and AT:N apply because the documented path requires no target-specific secret, enforced safeguard bypass, or independent execution condition; model acceptance is the exploit's uncertain outcome, not a separate deployment requirement. The attacker owns the submitted invoice content, but not the application's payment-approval authority: finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:409-443 supports serious integrity loss in the agent decision and subsequent database approval state, while this path establishes no confidentiality or availability loss and no actual external funds transfer.\"\n  },\n  \"evidence\": {\n    \"LC\": [\n      \"finbot-ctf-demo/src/routes/vendor.py:69-110\",\n      \"finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:363-407\",\n      \"finbot-ctf-demo/docs/FinBot-CTF-walkthrough-goal-manipulation.md:136-150\"\n    ],\n    \"CP\": [\n      \"finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:163-166\",\n      \"finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:363-407\",\n      \"finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:347-361\",\n      \"finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:735-748\"\n    ],\n    \"AP\": [\n      \"finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:347-361\",\n      \"finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:409-443\",\n      \"finbot-ctf-demo/docs/FinBot-CTF-walkthrough-goal-manipulation.md:136-150\"\n    ],\n