 \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n    \"rationale\": \"The supplied default deployment manifest does not provision an OpenAI API key in finbot-ctf-demo/render.yaml:1-17. On that uncredentialed default, client initialization fails as handled in finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:14-21, and the rule-based fallback described at finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:772-877 makes fixed decisions rather than model-directed action choices; an externally supplied key would change this assessment.\"\n  },\n  \"applicability_as_modeled\": {\n    \"model_directed_goal_pursuit\": true,\n    \"selects_or_sequences_actions\": true,\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"rationale\": \"The documented agent pursues natural-language invoice-processing goals and uses automatic model-selected tool calls over an iterative loop, as described at finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:32-99 and finbot-ctf-demo/src/services/finbot_agent.py:150-226. The documented attack specifically relies on changing those priorities and inducing an approval action in finbot-ctf-demo/docs/FinBot-CTF-walkthrough-goal-manipulation.md:136-150.\"\n  },\n  \"refusal\": null\n}",
